From: mscharged-port
Subject: Transport original script VM address words natively
Upstream-base: f75ccf1ad20e5bd7585962990db08067c0ae498a

The FuzzyAIRuntime VM stack holds Wii 32-bit words. Its native functions pop
object addresses from the stack and push returned addresses back. Use the
existing cached SDK word transport (EncodeVMAddress/DecodeVMAddress, as the
frontend and game presentation VMs do) for exactly the address-bearing words the
host compiler identifies; numeric and float words, the stack layout and all
interpreter control flow stay 32-bit and unchanged. FuzzyRuntimeBase decodes the
captured return variant word and ScriptMachine encodes its init-function
argument the same way. The retail no-op (142, 143) and identity (146) natives
never dereference their pointer-typed parameter, and scripts pass plain numbers
through them, so those words are carried unchanged instead of decoded. Console
builds keep the literal casts. (The game Presentation string natives are
transported by 0651.)

